SUMMARY:Ringo Starr & His All-Starr Band
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: $179 $259 $299 $369\nAMT Member Pre-Sale: Wednesday\, July 8 at 10:00 a.m.\nPublic On-Sale: Friday\, July 10 at 10:00 a.m. \nRingo Starr – VIP Ticket Package $542 each \n\n-One premium reserved ticket\n-Specially designed Ringo Starr and His All-Starr Band tour shirt\n-Collectible Ringo Starr tour lithograph\n-Ringo Starr tote bag\n-Exclusive Ringo Starr tour merchandise item\n-Commemorative tour laminate & lanyard\n-Commemorative ticket\n-Limited availability\n\nPackage Disclaimer for dates not on Ticketmaster national spec: \nBuyers will receive an email approximately three days prior to the show date with VIP details\, sent to the email address submitted at time of purchase. One More Time VIP\, the artist\, tour\, promoter\, ticketing company\, venue or any other affiliated parties are not responsible for outdated or inaccurate information provided by the consumer. All packages and package contents are non-transferable; no refunds or exchanges; all sales are final. Package elements are subject to change at any time without notice. VIP merchandise will ship directly to customers. Please note that items may arrive after the show. VIP purchasers will receive a separate email sent closer to the performance date with instructions on how to redeem their merchandise items through the One More Time VIP redemption site. If you have any questions regarding your VIP package elements\, please contact info@onemoretimevip.com.  \nFew artists have shaped popular music like Ringo Starr. A nine-time GRAMMY® Award winner and two-time Rock & Roll Hall of Fame inductee — first as a member of The Beatles and later as a solo artist — Ringo’s legendary career has made him one of the most beloved figures in rock & roll. \nRingo Starr & His All-Starr Band brings that legacy to the stage with an extraordinary lineup of hitmakers\, including Steve Lukather of Toto\, Colin Hay of Men at Work\, Warren Ham of Kansas\, Toto\, and Bloodrock\, Hamish Stuart of Average White Band and Paul McCartney’s band\, acclaimed drummer Gregg Bissonette\, and Buck Johnson of Aerosmith and Hollywood Vampires. \nFans can expect an unforgettable night of Ringo’s solo favorites\, Beatles classics\, and hits from the All-Starr Band members themselves — all delivered with the spirit\, musicianship\, and “Peace and Love” that define Ringo Starr. \nDon’t miss this rare opportunity to see a living legend joined by an incredible band of all-stars live in concert. \nFor certain concerts\, audience members may prefer to stand or dance\, especially when encouraged by the artist to do so. Guest expectations differ\, so we simply ask all attendees to extend mutual respect toward one another and maintain awareness of those around them. Our staff will only intervene in matters of safety or when behavior is deemed unruly\, combative\, or disruptive to the overall performance.
URL:https://amtshows.com/show/ringo-starr-his-all-starr-band/
LOCATION:American Music Theatre\, 2425 Lincoln Hwy East\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17605\, United States
CATEGORIES:Celebrity Concerts
